I see exactly why that is happening! When you applied the updates earlier, you successfully added the 3-character rule to the searchBranches function, but it looks like the searchCgls function was accidentally skipped. It is still checking for length === 0.
Let's fix that specific function so it strictly requires 3 characters before hitting your backend API.
### Fix the searchCgls Function
Find the searchCgls function definition (around line 225 in your file).
**Find this exact block:**
```javascript
  const searchCgls = useCallback(
    debounce(async (query, rowId) => {
      if (!query || query.trim().length === 0) {
        setCglSearch({ loadingId: null, options: [] });
        return;
      }
      setCglSearch((prev) => ({ ...prev, loadingId: rowId }));

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
  const searchCgls = useCallback(
    debounce(async (query, rowId) => {
      // Changed from === 0 to < 3 to enforce the minimum character limit
      if (!query || query.trim().length < 3) {
        setCglSearch({ loadingId: null, options: [] });
        return;
      }
      setCglSearch((prev) => ({ ...prev, loadingId: rowId }));

```
Once you make this single line change, the CGL dropdown will behave exactly like the Branch dropdown and will wait until you type at least 3 characters before attempting to search!
